          "heading": "Planet Rugby expects France to hammer Jake White's Fiji in Lyon",
          "body": "Planet Rugby's preview says France will use their attacking game to beat Jake White's side in Lyon, while risking a 'soft underbelly' before the South Africa test six days later. The news behind it is the selection: Antoine Dupont and Romain Ntamack start together at half-back for the first time since March 2025, a 20-month gap, with Matthieu Jalibert out injured. For Fiji, the piece recalls Mick Byrne leaving in April and Senirusi Seruvakula serving as interim coach through July before White was appointed."
