          "kicker": "Turin rout",
          "heading": "Italy crumble to 66-7 defeat as Springboks run in nine tries",
          "body": "Italy lost 66-7 to South Africa on Saturday, conceding nine tries, their fourth straight defeat, and were 45-0 down at half-time. Head coach Gonzalo Quesada's side went into the match without 16 players, including captain Michele Lamaro and centres Tommaso Menoncello and Juan Ignacio Brex. Sacha Feinberg-Mngomezulu was the Springboks' standout, scoring a solo try and kicking 21 points, while the world champions moved alone to the top of the Southern Hemisphere standings."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
