    "390": {
      "date": "2026-11-08",
      "edition": "Sunday 8 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Ashman hat-trick",
          "heading": "Ewan Ashman hat-trick not enough as Scotland fade against All Blacks",
          "body": "Ewan Ashman's three first-half tries gave Scotland a chance at Murrayfield, but the hooker's hat-trick was the lone high point of a day that slipped away after the interval. Scotland failed to score in the second half as New Zealand added three tries, one from Beauden Barrett, and Planet Rugby noted Ashman became the first Scotsman to score a hat-trick against the All Blacks. Head coach Gregor Townsend said: \"And it wasn't there today. So that's frustrating.\" Scotland's next match is against Australia."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
