      }
    },
    "391": {
      "date": "2026-11-08",
      "edition": "Sunday 8 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Coaching verdict",
          "heading": "Steve Tandy admits Wales need vast improvement despite Japan win",
          "body": "Wales had to hold on in Cardiff, beating Japan 28-21 for a bonus-point win and their second of the autumn. Archie Griffin opened the scoring inside four minutes, and Josh Adams went on to score twice, with Louis Rees-Zammit also over. Kenta Fukuda's 75th-minute try kept Japan within a score until Adams claimed a turnover penalty with seconds left. It was Tandy's fourth win in 13 Tests in charge, watched by a sparse crowd at the Millennium Stadium."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Scotland fade against All Blacks despite Ashman hat-trick",
