      "date": "2026-11-08",
      "edition": "Sunday 8 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Pay dispute",
          "heading": "Rugby Australia writes directly to Wallabies players over pay, bypassing union",
          "body": "Negotiations for a new collective agreement are not going well, and the Wallabies are heading into Sunday's Test with the dispute unresolved. Rupa president Tom Robertson said he was disappointed the offer went straight to players, \"particularly while the Wallabies are on tour\". Rugby Australia chair Daniel Herbert responded that Rupa's counter-proposals \"threaten the future of the game in Australia\". The two Bledisloe Cup defeats by New Zealand were the last Tests under the 2023 agreement."
        },
