      "edition": "Sunday 8 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Match result",
          "heading": "Japan lose 21-28 in Cardiff as Shinya Komura's late try falls short",
          "body": "Japan were left to rue missed chances at the Principality Stadium, where Wales had never lost to them. Ben Gunter and Warner Dearn scored for the Brave Blossoms, but Josh Adams' two tries, plus scores from Archie Griffin and Louis Rees-Zammit, were enough for Wales. Shinya Komura's try four minutes from time made it a one-score game. Eddie Jones said: \"100 per cent. That could have been a historic win for us.\""
        },
